/renovate-prs

You are running unattended, from a daily systemd timer on {{ inventory_hostname }}. Nobody
is watching this session and nobody can answer a question, so decide and act rather than
asking. Follow the renovate-prs skill; the notes below govern where it and this run differ.

Scope for this run:

- Nominate at most {{ pins.max_prs }} PRs to land; the runner lands no more than that. The
  timer runs daily, so the rest wait for tomorrow. Take them in the order the skill's triage
  puts them: the mechanical classes first (uv.lock, prek/CI tooling, plain k8s image pins), the
  `manual — ` work orders last.
- The session has a wall-clock ceiling of {{ pins.session_timeout_s }}s and a spend ceiling of
  ${{ pins.budget_usd }}. Hitting either kills the session mid-step and the runner carries out
  no request, so finish writing them well inside the limit.
- You are already inside a git worktree at .claude/worktrees/{{ renovate_agent_worktree }} of
  your own clone, {{ renovate_agent_clone_dir }}, reset to origin/master for this run. You run
  as {{ renovate_agent_user }}: your GitHub token can only read. It cannot comment on, close
  or re-run a PR, push, merge or file an issue, and you cannot deploy.

How you close, comment on or re-run a PR, which replaces every `gh pr close`, `gh pr comment`
and `gh run rerun` step in the skill:

- Write one JSON file per request into `/var/lib/renovate-agent/requests/`, with the Write
  tool. The runner carries each one out with its own token after this session ends, and
  records the outcome. Do not wait for it, and do not call `gh` to do it yourself.
  - `{"action": "close", "pr": <n>, "body": "Superseded by #<m>."}`
  - `{"action": "comment", "pr": <n>, "body": "<text>"}`
  - `{"action": "rerun", "pr": <n>}` re-runs the failed checks at the PR's head.
  - `{"action": "land", "pr": <n>}` nominates the PR for landing; see below.
- Only an open Renovate PR this run counted is accepted, a body is at most 4000 characters,
  and a file over 16 KiB is refused. Name the files `<n>-<action>.json`.
- In the summary, say which requests you wrote. A PR you asked to close is not closed yet.

How a PR lands, which replaces every `land.sh` step in the skill:

- You do not land anything. Write a `land` request for each PR the skill would land, in the
  order you want them landed; files are carried out in name order, so prefix the name with its
  place, such as `1-<n>-land.json`. Do not start the lander yourself.
- After this session ends, the runner lands the nominations one at a time through
  `renovate-agent-land@<n>`, which re-checks each PR itself: Renovate's author, a `renovate/`
  branch into master, no denied role, no `inventory/` change, a passed stability soak and a
  bounded file count. The runner goes on to the next nomination after a settled landing, a
  landing with nothing to deploy, or the lander's own refusal, and stops after anything else.
- So nominate only PRs you have checked are ready, and say in the summary which you nominated
  and why. The digest reports how each landing ended.

Stop conditions, which are outcomes and not failures:

- Anything `CLAUDE.md` → *When to wait* covers. Report which one and leave the PR open.
- A `manual — ` work order. Finishing one means pushing a commit, which your token cannot do.
  Read what it asks for and put the hand-off in the summary: the PR, what the work is, and any
  blocker you found in the release notes (an upgrade plan, a DB format migration, a breaking
  change).
- A PR whose title OR BRANCH carries `k8s_autodeploy: false`, wherever in the parenthetical it
  sits — the denylist rule leads with it, and a per-package rule ends with it after its own work
  order (the crowdsec bouncer plugin, meilisearch, karakeep's time-tagger deps, n8n). Read both
  with one call, `gh pr list --author app/renovate --json number,title,headRefName`: Renovate
  drops the group name from the title of a group holding ONE dependency and titles it `Update
  <dep> …` instead, so for some of these PRs the marker survives only in the branch, slugified
  as `k8s_autodeploy-false` (#2641). #2620 was a denied role's pin titled `Update
  klutchell/unbound Docker tag to v1.26.1`, and its branch is what named it. Every rule
  carrying the marker sets `groupSingleUpdates: true` since #2646 and #2654, so newer PRs carry
  the marker in the title as well; a PR raised before that can still title bare,
  which is why the branch stays the tell you must read. That phrase
  is not a work order for you, and neither is the one in front of it: it marks a role whose
  failed deploy the health gate cannot see (authelia's middleware answers before the backend,
  traefik's outage leaves the host probes green), so the review its denial asks for is a
  person, and the runner's gated land is not that person. Do not nominate it. Name it in the summary with the command an interactive session
  runs: `./scripts/deploy_tools/land.sh --pr <n> --arm-merge --await-merge --detach && cc-wait land <n>`,
  the `land-after-merge` skill's invocation.

You cannot file a finding, so the summary is the only hand-off. Give every PR you leave open its
reason there. This session's transcript is read only when the digest already says something
went wrong, so a reason left out of the summary reaches nobody.

Finish with a plain summary: which PRs you nominated to land, which you left and why (a
`k8s_autodeploy: false` PR with its `land.sh` command, a `manual — ` work order with its
hand-off), and which you asked to close. A Renovate PR you asked to close as superseded is not
